  "query_preview": "..\n(Tomorrow through Monday)\nIssued at 1110 AM CDT Mon Aug 3 2026\n\nAbove normal temperatures make a return on Tuesday, along with\nheat index values that will be marginal for a Heat Advisory in the\nwarmer locales. No advisory will be issued with this package given\nthe spotty nature of the forecast 105 heat indices, instead\nchoosing to let later shifts get another look at it before\ntomorrow. Tuesday night and into Wednesday, a weak cold front will\napproach the Kansas border before becoming quasi-stationary. This\nfront will serve as a focus for isolated to widely scattered\nshowers and storms on Wednesday afternoon, as well as leading to\nwarmer temperatures on Wednesday due to pre-frontal warming. Heat\nheadlines will likely be needed on Wednesday. The front will move\ninto portions of the area on Thursday, leading to shower and\nthunderstorm chances southward to near I-40 during the afternoon\nand slightly cooler temperatures. Shower and thunderstorm chances\nlook to peak Thursday night into Friday, with Friday also likely\nto be the coolest day of the period. Upper level high pressure\nover the southwestern United States will extend eastward into the\nCentral Plains for the weekend and into early next week, bringing\na return to largely dry conditions and above normal temperatures.",
